1
00:00:01,303 --> 00:00:01,952
RenewFlow.

2
00:00:01,952 --> 00:00:06,950
An agent that renews insurance on the channel each customer actually answers.

3
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:13,506
Everything you will see is synthetic, and WhatsApp and email are simulated locally in this recording.

4
00:00:14,111 --> 00:00:19,935
Renewals are predictable revenue, and insurers lose them to one-size-fits-all reminders.

5
00:00:19,935 --> 00:00:25,097
RenewFlow chooses the channel, holds the conversation, and knows when to stop.

6
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:28,269
Meet Priya.

7
00:00:28,269 --> 00:00:34,022
Her premium is up from fourteen thousand eight hundred rupees to eighteen thousand four hundred.

8
00:00:34,022 --> 00:00:38,876
Her history says she reads WhatsApp and ignores email, so that is where we start.

9
00:00:38,876 --> 00:00:43,311
The scores come from her last ninety days, and consent always comes first.

10
00:00:43,816 --> 00:00:44,401
One click.

11
00:00:44,401 --> 00:00:49,960
The agent picks the channel, looks up the policy, sends the message, and schedules a follow up.

12
00:00:50,465 --> 00:00:53,601
Every step is recorded, including the raw tool calls.

13
00:00:55,735 --> 00:00:58,913
Now we play Priya, and ask whether she can split the payment.

14
00:01:00,844 --> 00:01:05,753
The agent explains exactly why the premium went up, and prices a quarterly plan.

15
00:01:05,753 --> 00:01:12,258
Every rupee amount comes from a pricing tool, and a guardrail blocks any number the tools did not produce.

16
00:01:12,764 --> 00:01:15,179
She asks for the details by email.

17
00:01:15,179 --> 00:01:18,588
Same conversation, new channel, no lost context.

18
00:01:19,093 --> 00:01:21,820
The quote arrives with a secure payment link.

19
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:25,941
She pays, the policy is renewed, and she gets a receipt on WhatsApp.

20
00:01:26,512 --> 00:01:29,616
A different customer writes about a rejected claim.

21
00:01:29,616 --> 00:01:32,721
Claims and complaints are never handled by the bot.

22
00:01:32,721 --> 00:01:35,643
It hands over with a summary, then stays silent.

23
00:01:36,148 --> 00:01:39,582
A person sees the summary and picks it up with full context.

24
00:01:40,275 --> 00:01:46,653
When a customer sends STOP, consent is revoked on every channel immediately, before the model is involved.

25
00:01:50,796 --> 00:01:54,535
Now twenty synthetic customers run through the same agent.

26
00:01:54,535 --> 00:01:59,756
Renewal rate, revenue secured, guardrail activity, and how each channel performs.

27
00:02:00,361 --> 00:02:04,243
Each customer is placed on the channel they are most likely to answer.

28
00:02:04,783 --> 00:02:14,340
Under the hood, WhatsApp goes through AWS End User Messaging Social, email through Amazon S E S, and reasoning runs on Amazon Bedrock.

29
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:21,542
Every channel sits behind an adapter, so the product also runs offline, as it does in this recording.

30
00:02:21,542 --> 00:02:22,255
Thank you.
